(7653206, 1245284, 251422, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ammie:</b></div><hr/><i> O wow! </i></td></tr></table> He was such a cool subject!</td>', 'Originally posted by Ammie: O wow!  He was such a cool subject!', '2020-02-10 07:19:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7653207, 1245284, 30049, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Beaubeau:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Great photo, Im wondering if the background is legal? Anyway time will tell. </i></td></tr></table>Thank you. The Background is just a texture but who knows- it was fun to do and i like the shot.  The feathers actually looked like that - it''s not the texture.  I checked back on the original photo.  Thanks for your comments. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Interesting.  If the background is a "texture" then wouldn''t it be applied to the entire image?  I''m still unclear on how the whole texture stuff (rules) apply.</td>', 'Originally posted by Beaubeau: Originally posted by Neat: Great photo, Im wondering if the background is legal? Anyway time will tell. Thank you. The Background is just a texture but who knows- it was fun to do and i like the shot.  The feathers actually looked like that - it''s not the texture.  I checked back on the original photo.  Thanks for your comments.  Interesting.  If the background is a "texture" then wouldn''t it be applied to the entire image?  I''m still unclear on how the whole texture stuff (rules) apply.', '2020-02-10 07:46:48.000000', NULL, 0),
