(7653288, 1245284, 156466, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Beaubeau:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Great photo, Im wondering if the background is legal? Anyway time will tell. </i></td></tr></table>Thank you. The Background is just a texture but who knows- it was fun to do and i like the shot.  The feathers actually looked like that - it''s not the texture.  I checked back on the original photo.  Thanks for your comments. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Interesting.  If the background is a "texture" then wouldn''t it be applied to the entire image?  I''m still unclear on how the whole texture stuff (rules) apply. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Alas the minute I saw this I asked myself the same question about legality and only bring it up hear since it''s already been asked. The removal of unwanted objects bullet in the Standard Rules tells me that this is likely not kosher. But I''ll say this, it''s a brilliant job on the replacement.</td>', 'Originally posted by glad2badad: Originally posted by Beaubeau: Originally posted by Neat: Great photo, Im wondering if the background is legal? Anyway time will tell. Thank you. The Background is just a texture but who knows- it was fun to do and i like the shot.  The feathers actually looked like that - it''s not the texture.  I checked back on the original photo.  Thanks for your comments.  Interesting.  If the background is a "texture" then wouldn''t it be applied to the entire image?  I''m still unclear on how the whole texture stuff (rules) apply.   Alas the minute I saw this I asked myself the same question about legality and only bring it up hear since it''s already been asked. The removal of unwanted objects bullet in the Standard Rules tells me that this is likely not kosher. But I''ll say this, it''s a brilliant job on the replacement.', '2020-02-11 10:07:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(7653291, 1245284, 251422, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Beaubeau:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Great photo, Im wondering if the background is legal? Anyway time will tell. </i></td></tr></table>Thank you. The Background is just a texture but who knows- it was fun to do and i like the shot.  The feathers actually looked like that - it''s not the texture.  I checked back on the original photo.  Thanks for your comments. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Interesting.  If the background is a "texture" then wouldn''t it be applied to the entire image?  I''m still unclear on how the whole texture stuff (rules) apply. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Who knows - time will tell but the texture is applied over the background - you don''t have to apply texture to the entire image and it doesn''t have to be applied at 100% either.  The background is underneath the texture -I appreciate your comments though.  I''m new to the community but enjoying it.  Thanks for the feedback.</td>', 'Originally posted by glad2badad: Originally posted by Beaubeau: Originally posted by Neat: Great photo, Im wondering if the background is legal? Anyway time will tell. Thank you. The Background is just a texture but who knows- it was fun to do and i like the shot.  The feathers actually looked like that - it''s not the texture.  I checked back on the original photo.  Thanks for your comments.  Interesting.  If the background is a "texture" then wouldn''t it be applied to the entire image?  I''m still unclear on how the whole texture stuff (rules) apply.   Who knows - time will tell but the texture is applied over the background - you don''t have to apply texture to the entire image and it doesn''t have to be applied at 100% either.  The background is underneath the texture -I appreciate your comments though.  I''m new to the community but enjoying it.  Thanks for the feedback.', '2020-02-11 11:54:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7653293, 1245284, 251422, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JakeKurdsjuk:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Beaubeau:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Great photo, Im wondering if the background is legal? Anyway time will tell. </i></td></tr></table>Thank you. The Background is just a texture but who knows- it was fun to do and i like the shot.  The feathers actually looked like that - it''s not the texture.  I checked back on the original photo.  Thanks for your comments. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Interesting.  If the background is a "texture" then wouldn''t it be applied to the entire image?  I''m still unclear on how the whole texture stuff (rules) apply. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Alas the minute I saw this I asked myself the same question about legality and only bring it up hear since it''s already been asked. The removal of unwanted objects bullet in the Standard Rules tells me that this is likely not kosher. But I''ll say this, it''s a brilliant job on the replacement. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well technically nothing was removed...Texture is applied over the image  But thanks for your feedback!</td>', 'Originally posted by JakeKurdsjuk: Originally posted by glad2badad: Originally posted by Beaubeau: Originally posted by Neat: Great photo, Im wondering if the background is legal? Anyway time will tell. Thank you. The Background is just a texture but who knows- it was fun to do and i like the shot.  The feathers actually looked like that - it''s not the texture.  I checked back on the original photo.  Thanks for your comments.  Interesting.  If the background is a "texture" then wouldn''t it be applied to the entire image?  I''m still unclear on how the whole texture stuff (rules) apply.   Alas the minute I saw this I asked myself the same question about legality and only bring it up hear since it''s already been asked. The removal of unwanted objects bullet in the Standard Rules tells me that this is likely not kosher. But I''ll say this, it''s a brilliant job on the replacement.   Well technically nothing was removed...Texture is applied over the image  But thanks for your feedback!', '2020-02-11 13:22:44.000000', NULL, 0),
